<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Vietnamese (vi) for :feature:device. Mirrors values/strings.xml key for key.

  WORDING BAN (LLM.md §1, §5) carries into every locale, and this cluster is where it bites hardest:
  the competitor's device and battery screens are exactly where its performance claims live. Not one
  string below says the app will speed anything up, free memory, extend battery life, or improve
  anything by any percentage. Every string here either NAMES a reading or REPORTS one with its unit.

  The second rule holds too: no state carries a formatted string, so every %1$s below is filled at
  render time by rememberByteFormat() or a stringResource — never by a ViewModel.

  The third: a value that could not be read says so. value_unavailable is used wherever the
  competitor substitutes a constant.
-->
